ipes</li><li>Water losses</li></ul></div>

<h2>A city that knows tornadoes</h2>
<p>On November 17, 2013, a late-season outbreak spawned tornadoes across Indiana, including in Kokomo. Less than three years later, on August 24, 2016, a strong tornado tore through the south side of the city, damaging homes, apartments and businesses along a several-mile path. Those two events, plus the regular spring hail and wind seasons, mean many Kokomo homes have been through at least one significant claim.</p>
<h2>Housing in Kokomo</h2>
<p>The Old Silk Stocking Historic District holds large early-20th-century homes built during Kokomo’s automotive and industrial boom. Surrounding neighborhoods include factory-era bungalows and cottages, followed by mid-century ranches and newer subdivisions on the west and south sides. Russiaville, Greentown and rural Howard County add farmhouses and outbuildings.</p>
<h2>Disputes we see in Kokomo</h2>
<ul>
<li>Repeat-storm homes where carriers argue damage predates the current loss.</li>
<li>Tornado-damaged homes where the repair-versus-rebuild decision is contested.</li>
<li>Apartment and commercial claims with multiple buildings along a tornado path.</li>
<li>Outbuildings and detached garages under-valued on rural properties.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Communities we cover</h2>
<p>Kokomo, Russiaville, Greentown, Galveston, Tipton, Peru and surrounding Howard, Tipton and Miami counties.</p>

<h2>Appraisal services in Kokomo</h2>
<p>Every Indiana Insurance Appraiser service is available to property owners in Kokomo and the rest of Howard County, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/indiana-claim-appraisal/appraisal-clause-appraiser/">Appraisal Clause Representation</a></li><li><a href="/indiana-claim-appraisal/home-insurance-claim-appraisal/">Homeowner Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/indiana-claim-appraisal/commercial-hoa-claim-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/indiana-claim-appraisal/hail-roof-damage-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/indiana-claim-appraisal/tornado-wind-damage-appraisal/">Tornado &amp; Wind Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/indiana-claim-appraisal/water-damage-claim-appraisal/">Water Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/indiana-claim-appraisal/fire-smoke-damage-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Damage Appraisal</a></li></ul>
<h2>Questions from Kokomo property owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>My home was repaired after 2016. Can the carrier blame new damage on that storm?</summary><div class="a"><p>Carriers sometimes argue that damage is old. Records of the earlier repairs, dated photos and evidence specific to the new storm help separate the two.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is a partly destroyed home a total loss?</summary><div class="a"><p>Not automatically. The question is whether repair, including code work and hidden structural damage, would cost more than rebuilding. That’s an amount-of-loss question appraisal can address.</p></div></details></div>
